# Alo King AI Menu Extraction, Order Tracking, and Zone Activation Strategy

## Executive decision

Alo King should launch ordering through a **zone activation system**, not simply switch ordering on for every imported vendor.

A zone becomes orderable only when all of the following are true:

```text
At least one verified merchant with a live menu
+ at least one active, trained, dispatchable driver
+ a configured delivery route/fee
+ a support and exception process
+ a tested customer notification path
```

The system must keep three concepts separate:

```text
Directory visibility: people can discover the business
Ordering availability: customers can place an order
Live dispatch coverage: Alo King can fulfil the order now
```

The AI menu extractor should turn uploaded images, PDFs, and WhatsApp media into a **reviewable draft**, never directly into a live menu. The order tracker should combine server-side order events, driver GPS, route-aware ETA, and clear fallback messaging. Lebanon’s irregular addresses, village landmarks, mobile coverage gaps, and mountain roads require more than a generic map pin.

---

# 1. End-to-end architecture

```text
Merchant claim through WhatsApp or portal
→ identity and permission verification
→ upload menu media
→ secure file storage and malware/type checks
→ OCR / PDF text extraction
→ vision-language menu extraction
→ normalization and duplicate detection
→ price and currency interpretation
→ merchant review and confirmation
→ allergen/option review
→ menu publication
→ merchant live-ordering gate
→ zone readiness check
→ customer ordering enabled
→ driver dispatch
→ live tracking and delivery events
```

The system should use a shared backend for portal and merchant WhatsApp. The channel changes; the business rules do not.

