# 5. Lebanese menu-specific rules

## 5.1 Currency interpretation

The extractor must distinguish:

```text
$6
6 USD
600,000 L.L.
600
600k
6,000,000
```

Never assume that a bare number is USD.

If prices look like LBP thousands, show the merchant the interpretation:

> I think `450` means **450,000 LBP**, not 450 LBP. Is that correct?

A price conversion requires:

```text
source_currency
source_value
exchange_rate_at_confirmation
normalized_price_usd
normalized_price_lbp
rounding_policy
```

The merchant must confirm currency and any thousands multiplier before publication.

## 5.2 Arabic and English names

Keep the merchant’s original name and a normalized display name. Never remove Arabic from a Lebanese menu simply because the English translation is available.

Allow:

```text
name_ar
name_en
name_original
search_aliases
```

Search aliases can include transliterations such as:

```text
shawarma
shawrma
shawerma
شاورما
```

## 5.3 Options and modifiers

Extract separately:

```text
size
bread
sauce
protein
side
extra
removal
combo choice
```

Required options must block checkout until selected. Optional options must be clearly labelled.

## 5.4 Allergens

AI may extract allergens explicitly written on the menu. It must not certify that a dish is allergen-free from a vague description.

Use states:

```text
not_reviewed
merchant_listed
merchant_confirmed
platform_reviewed
```

Customer-facing allergy answers must distinguish:

> The menu lists sesame as an ingredient.

from:

> The restaurant confirms this item is safe for a sesame allergy.

