# 10. Driver location tracking

## 10.1 Location cadence

Recommended cadence:

```text
active en-route: every 10–15 seconds
near destination: every 5–10 seconds
waiting/idle: every 60–120 seconds or no tracking
weak battery/background: adaptive lower frequency
```

The driver app should send location only for active assignments and only while the driver is on shift or carrying an order.

## 10.2 Location quality

Store:

```text
latitude
longitude
accuracy_meters
heading
speed
captured_at
received_at
battery_level, optional
network_state, optional
```

Reject or flag impossible jumps:

- location accuracy too poor;
- timestamp too old;
- speed impossible for the vehicle/road;
- jump across incompatible routes;
- location outside the active delivery corridor.

## 10.3 Privacy controls

- stop high-frequency tracking after delivery;
- retain only what operations and legal policy require;
- limit staff access;
- do not use driver location for unrelated advertising;
- explain location use to drivers;
- support location pause only when no active delivery is in progress, except emergencies.

