# 11. Route-aware ETA

The current UI calculates a simple distance-based ETA. For Lebanon, production ETA should use road-aware estimates.

## 11.1 ETA inputs

```text
driver location
restaurant location
customer location
actual road route
road distance
ridge/valley route
terrain/elevation
vehicle type
current traffic/incident data if available
restaurant readiness
batch stops
historical route time
GPS freshness
```

Never display a precise-looking ETA from stale or straight-line data.

## 11.2 ETA output

Show an honest range:

```text
Arriving in about 20–30 minutes
```

Use a narrower ETA only when:

- GPS is fresh;
- route is known;
- food is collected;
- the driver is not carrying an incompatible batch;
- the route confidence is high.

## 11.3 Mountain-road logic

Alo King should maintain route metadata for village pairs:

```text
ridge_zone
road_distance_km
expected_minutes_by_vehicle
ascent_meters
descent_meters
valley_crossing_penalty
road_quality
seasonal_risk
night_risk
```

Reject routes that look close by coordinates but require an inefficient or unsafe valley crossing.

## 11.4 Stale GPS behavior

If the last location is older than the threshold:

> The driver’s live location is temporarily delayed due to weak signal. The latest estimated arrival is **[range]**.

Do not animate a moving marker from stale data as if it were real-time.

