# 13. Zone activation strategy for Lebanon

## 13.1 Zone is a first-class operational entity

Do not treat `delivery_village` as a free-text string. Create:

```text
service_zones
service_zone_aliases
service_zone_boundaries
zone_route_matrix
zone_coverage_snapshots
zone_activation_events
```

A zone may be:

- a village;
- a neighborhood;
- a route corridor;
- a delivery ring around a verified hub.

Use normalized zone IDs with Arabic and English aliases.

## 13.2 Zone states

```text
planned
researching
directory_only
merchant_ready
driver_ready
soft_launch
active
capacity_limited
paused_weather
paused_no_driver
paused_no_merchant
suspended_quality
retired
```

## 13.3 Zone activation gate

A zone becomes `active` only when:

### Merchant requirement

- at least one merchant is verified;
- merchant has a complete live menu;
- prices and hours are confirmed;
- merchant can receive and accept orders;
- merchant has an operational contact;
- substitution/cancellation policy is configured.

### Driver requirement

- at least one trained driver is verified;
- driver has an approved vehicle;
- driver is available for the intended service window;
- route and delivery fee are configured;
- cash/online payment process is ready;
- tracking test has passed.

### Platform requirement

- customer ordering flow tested;
- merchant alert tested;
- dispatch assignment tested;
- order tracking link tested;
- support path tested;
- exception and cancellation paths tested;
- zone capacity limits configured.

## 13.4 Two levels of activation

### Soft launch

Use when:

- one verified merchant exists;
- one driver exists but supply is limited;
- support is actively monitoring;
- order volume is capped.

Soft launch rules:

- invite-only or limited customer exposure;
- one order per driver;
- limited hours;
- no complex batching;
- manual dispatch oversight;
- daily review.

### Full active zone

Use when:

- merchant coverage is reliable;
- driver coverage covers peak windows;
- tracking and support are stable;
- failure rates are within thresholds;
- enough capacity exists for expected demand.

